# Official links only

- A public listing may link only to the employer's own page (apply URL,
  careers page or first-party ATS host). Job boards, aggregators, Google News
  wrappers, fundsforngos, indiawaterportal and similar are **discovery only**.
- Never store a blocklisted/aggregator URL in a public field. Drop the lead or
  resolve it to the employer page first.
- `apply_url`, `org_website` and `org_domain` come from the verified page plus
  `public/employers.json` — never from the LLM.
- Anything that is not `verification_level == "page_verified"` is quarantined
  (`status: "quarantined"`), never published and never deleted.
- Title, deadline, compensation, qualifications and every must-have skill must
  appear on the fetched page (exact or fuzzy ≥ 0.9). Otherwise quarantine with
  `FIELD_NOT_IN_SOURCE`.
- Do not weaken `verify_link` (no `verify=False`, no blocklist bypass, no
  Playwright-only fallback that skips content checks).
- Never add a domain to `public/employers.json` without fetching it and
  confirming it is that organisation's own site.
- Front end: dossier URLs only; archived records render no outbound link;
  quarantined and `entry_type: "unknown"` records are hidden everywhere.
- Before committing: `python -m pytest tests -q`, `python scripts/link_guard.py`.
  Before deploying: `npm run build` then
  `python scripts/link_guard.py --dist dist`.
- Full policy and remediation runbook: `docs/LINK_POLICY.md`.
